<title>SWITZERLAND: Soros says rate of change of dollar may be worry.</title>
<headline>Soros says rate of change of dollar may be worry.</headline>
<dateline>DAVOS, Switzerland 1996-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financier George Soros said that the rate of change of the dollar could be worrying for G7 Finance Ministers when they meet in Berlin next Saturday.</p>
<p>Soros, who was speaking at news conference at the World Economic Forum, said that it was the pace of change rather the level of the U.S. currency that could be cause for concern.  </p>
<p>&quot;I don't see any great disturbance,&quot; Soros said, referring to the currency market.</p>
<p>But the rate of change of the dollar had accelerated and &quot;this could be a matter of concern (for the G7),&quot; he said in answer to a question.</p>
<p>--Davos newsroom 41 81 1449</p>
</text>
